#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# cancel

#% text
# `cancel(e)` writes each term of `e` in lowest terms, cancelling the common factors of its numerator and denominator.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Sums of fractions are not brought over a common denominator; use `together` for that.

#% item
# `cancel` works over the rationals and treats non-polynomial subexpressions as variables.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
cancel((x^2 - 1)/(x - 1))
#% output
#= 1 + x

#% cell
cancel((x^3 - y^3)/(x - y))
#% output
#= x*y + x^2 + y^2

#% cell
cancel((x^2 + 2*x + 1)/(x^2 - 1))
#% output
#= (1 + x)/(-1 + x)

#% cell
cancel((sin(x)^2 - 1)/(sin(x) + 1))
#% output
#= -1 + sin(x)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Each term separately:

#% cell
cancel((x^2 - 1)/(x + 1) + (x^2 - 4)/(x - 2))
#% output
#= 1 + 2*x

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `together` combines the terms, `cancel` does not:

#% cell
e = 1/(x - 1) - 1/(x + 1); [cancel(e), together(e)]
#% output
#= [-1/(1 + x) + (-1 + x)^-1, 2/(-1 + x^2)]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `together`, `factor`, `apart`, `simplify`, `polynomial_gcd`
